{"id":251359207008134,"type":"album","name":"Mental Notes","artist":"Split Enz","year":1975,"weight":11,"info":{"cover":"https://dn710606.ca.archive.org/0/items/mbid-27b3a589-ae43-3b85-a3f1-082e56a4441a/mbid-27b3a589-ae43-3b85-a3f1-082e56a4441a-9707237626.jpg","scaruffi":7.0,"yt":"emfK0ovEzjs","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/40kD3JoZgiQL0ZwH9OZ2Bg","youtube":"https://music.youtube.com/playlist?list=OLAK5uy_kdYt1Kd9xoXMfw_XDUIP_-kz8JkaCXrfY"},"desc":"The first proper Split Enz album features the band at its eccentric best. Mental Notes is completely noncommercial art rock filled with ambitious arrangements and slightly disturbing themes courtesy of the Phil Judd and Tim Finn songwriting partnership. Finn's bittersweet crooning perfectly complements Judd's madman persona on tracks like \"Stranger Than Fiction.\" Although the album would be repackaged, renamed, and re-recorded in years to come, the band would never again produce anything like it. -- Chris Woodstra (AMG) 4,5/5 Stars -- Credits Richard Batchens -- Engineer Jonathan Michael Chunn -- Bass, Guitar (Bass), Piano, Vocals (Background) Noel Crombie -- Drums, ."},"artist_ref":{"id":23858423134459,"name":"Split Enz","info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Split_Enz_%22Time_and_Tide%22_%281982_A%26M_publicity_photo%29.jpg?width=500"}},"labels":[],"genres":[{"id":191826593279813,"type":"genre","name":"Art Rock","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":531,"yt":null,"src":"musthear"}],"lists":[{"id":65232636722211,"name":"Scaruffi 1970s","src":"charts","grp":"Scaruffi","list_year":null,"rank":501,"year":1975,"note":null,"total":572,"scaruffi":7.0}],"podcast":[],"book_tracks":[{"id":251359207008134,"artist":"Split Enz","artist_id":23858423134459,"title":"Mental Notes","year":1975,"ess":1,"yt":"emfK0ovEzjs","kind":"a","book":{"id":8,"title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000","author":"Piero Scaruffi","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/scaruffi/"},"scene":"Techno-rock y pop de e